{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Establish a usable integrity baseline covering /etc on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"AIDE was configured to cover /etc, initialized with 1,703 entries, and returned a clean comparison after finalization. The root-owned mode-0600 database and clean check remained available after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d00f80f0ab0445b0","cmd-7840d27c8cfa4fcb","cmd-9e99c2f2ce1a4b34","cmd-a9e1f1cb13b545e4"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow later changes under /etc to be identified and reported.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded probe added under /etc was directly detected and reported as an added file, with AIDE's change-detected exit status. The probe was removed and the final baseline was verified clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0d6ef6681b4c4053","cmd-7840d27c8cfa4fcb"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.42,"summary":"No clearly unnecessary mutation was evidenced: installing and configuring AIDE, creating the baseline and timer, the reversible detection probe, final checks, and the mandated reboot all had task or verification roles. The initial unprivileged installation attempt showed permission failures without evidence of mutation. However, the privileged package transaction unpacked postfix before becoming stuck, and the corrective dpkg operation did not repair it; postfix remained seriously damaged in the final package-health snapshot. This is substantial executor-caused retained residue despite clean failed-service and socket observations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5a95e74ba1644d2d","cmd-aa57bab625514f90","cmd-9c5aacf331114488","cmd-75af164006c741da","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered system, timer, database, and clean AIDE state were observed; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree. Operational hygiene is materially degraded because postfix was left in a corrupted package state.","limitations":["The pre-restart external sha256sum of the protected database was denied, so byte-for-byte persistence was not compared using that command. Persistence is nevertheless strongly supported by identical AIDE database fingerprints and 1,703-entry clean checks before and after reboot.","The evidence demonstrates immediate reporting and a healthy enabled daily timer, but does not observe a naturally scheduled future timer execution. This does not undermine the contract's directly demonstrated ability to identify and report later changes."]}
